<item><title>Gabon prepares to split its state water and power utility by December</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-prepares-to-split-its-state-water-and-power-utility-6200d5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-prepares-to-split-its-state-water-and-power-utility-6200d5/</guid><category>Gabon</category><description>The government says no Gabonese employee should lose a job as officials work through contracts, debt and asset transfers before the split takes effect.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:26:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-prepares-to-split-its-state-water-and-power-utility-6200d5/share.jpg" length="43467" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-prepares-to-split-its-state-water-and-power-utility-6200d5/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Isuzu trains 24 Gabon truck drivers to cut breakdowns</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/isuzu-trains-24-gabon-truck-drivers-to-cut-breakdowns-f97a56/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/isuzu-trains-24-gabon-truck-drivers-to-cut-breakdowns-f97a56/</guid><category>Gabon</category><description>The two-day Libreville course covered driving, maintenance and road safety, with special attention to onboard systems many drivers did not know.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:21:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" length="31200" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gabon delivers first chicks to farms under poultry plan</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-delivers-first-chicks-to-farms-under-poultry-plan-9b1b43/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-delivers-first-chicks-to-farms-under-poultry-plan-9b1b43/</guid><category>Gabon</category><description>The agriculture minister received 37 600 day-old chicks in Libreville from a first order of 262 400 due to arrive by 17 December.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:06 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" length="31200" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gabon schedules vocational training entrance exam for 5 880 candidates</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-schedules-vocational-training-entrance-exam-for-5-880-6f920e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ga/gabon-schedules-vocational-training-entrance-exam-for-5-880-6f920e/</guid><category>Gabon</category><description>The public-centre exam was moved from 16 November to 21 November, with candidates sitting tests in mathematics, French and general knowledge.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:49:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" length="31200" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ga.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
